<title>FRANCE: Public transport strike in French city ends.</title>
<headline>Public transport strike in French city ends.</headline>
<dateline>ROUEN, France 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public transport workers in the French city of Rouen voted to end a 21-day strike on Wednesday, trade unions said.</p>
<p>Bus and metro drivers had been protesting against job cuts and for shorter working hours. Local authorities have agreed to reduce the working week to 34 hours instead of 38 from September next year and to create 90 jobs.</p>
<p>Unions said traffic should be back to normal from Thursday.</p>
</text>
